{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01BhMBBV5GuLS9rkeh6WZ2pr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the project's `CLAUDE.md` and supporting docs, here's what this project IS:\n\n- **It's a personal AI-agent research workspace** â€” John Liechty's \"Agentic Sandbox\" (`C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home`) for building, training, and evaluating clusters of AI agents. It's explicitly a *research project, not a production system*; most of its ~80 root markdown files are design docs (whitepapers, plans, session logs), with a smaller number of runnable-code folders.\n\n- **The shipped deliverable is a Next.js GUI** â€” the **Ghost World Labs (GWL-M) master GUI** (`sandbox-lab-gui/`), launched via `Launch-Ghost-World-Labs.bat`. It runs a custom Next.js + WebSocket server (`server.mjs`) on port 3001 that spawns and supervises agent terminals.\n\n- **Agents run on the OpenClaw runtime** â€” a globally-installed MIT-licensed npm package. The GUI dispatches turns through `agent-chat.mjs`, which reads per-agent provider/model from the canonical `Sandbox Setup Package/config/routing.json` and launches `openclaw agent` invocations.\n\n- **The active agent vehicle is `alpha-v0`** â€” a daily-use general-purpose \"t2r\" (tasteâ†’reason) agent routed through a custom dispatcher (`brain/dispatcher/t2r-dispatcher.mjs`), with a $100/month wallet cap and a 7-skill bundle. A registry of research/legacy agents lives behind a UI toggle.\n\n- **It ships a custom \"sovereign\" agent harness** â€” `gwl-t2r-brain/harness/`, a cache-stable ReAct loop with cost telemetry, tier-routing, compression, and provider portability (Anthropic/Google live; OpenAI/Grok key-gated). Recent work (the current `foreman/run` branch) added 6 default-OFF flag-gated orchestration waves.\n\n- **The long-game architecture is \"distill from frontier into small local students\"** â€” the gwl-server box's RTX 4070 (12 GB) is meant to QLoRA-fine-tune â‰¤8B local models, supporting a planned three-brain lineup: Opus-4.8 baseline, the efficient t2r brain, and a fully-local/sovereign OSS brain.\n\n- **It carries its own build/planning tooling** â€” a skill ecosystem (expert-coder, project-manager, research, etc.) linked from `skills-master/`, plus the Crucible (planning) â†’ Foreman (autonomous multi-wave build) pipeline, with Foreman-ready plan handoffs under `plans/foreman/`.\n\nOne caveat on grounding: these claims come from `CLAUDE.md` and the memory index, which are documentation â€” I haven't re-verified each path against the live filesystem in this turn. Want me to spot-check any specific claim (e.g., that the GUI server or harness code actually exists as described)?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7051,"cache_read_input_tokens":40827,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7051,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"981107f9-c214-473a-b7d4-2f0afc9ca751","uuid":"9ccac491-c34d-41b6-88a7-efe9a781054e","request_id":"req_011Cc38pgk23ZXr9KrqhXHkN"}
